---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import TrustBadges from '../../components/TrustBadges.astro';
import PricingCards from '../../components/PricingCards.astro';

const locale = 'en';
const page = 'pricing';

const title = 'Pricing and credit costs – Content Ninja';
const description =
  'Content Ninja pricing: HUF 34,990 + VAT per month with 500 renewing AI credits, or HUF 349,900 + VAT per year — 12 months for the price of 10, with 6,000 credits up front. See the detailed per-operation credit costs, the extra credit pack prices and how payment works.';
const keywords =
  'Content Ninja pricing, Content Ninja price, annual plan, AI credits, credit costs, credit consumption, extra credits, subscription, AI content generation cost';

// Buying credits and managing the subscription both start in the app (rather
// than via a direct Stripe link), so the user signs in to their account first.
const APP_URL = 'https://app.getcontentninja.com';

const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'How much does Content Ninja cost?',
    a: 'There is a single plan with two billing cycles. Monthly: HUF 34,990 + VAT per month (HUF 44,437 gross) with 500 renewing AI credits every month. Annual: HUF 349,900 + VAT per year (HUF 444,373 gross) — 12 months for the price of 10, with 6,000 credits granted in one go. Both include every module. If you book a demo you get HUF 17,495 + VAT off your first subscription term plus 250 bonus credits: that makes the first month HUF 17,495 + VAT (750 credits) on the monthly plan, or the first year HUF 332,405 + VAT (6,250 credits) on the annual plan.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How is the annual plan different from the monthly one?',
    a: 'In two ways. First, it is cheaper: you get 12 months for the price of 10, saving HUF 69,980 + VAT (HUF 88,871 gross) over a year. Second — and for many this matters more — there is no monthly ceiling: the 6,000 credits (exactly the same as 12×500) arrive in one go at the start of the term, and you spend them at your own pace within the 12 months. That means you can rewrite a 3,000-product catalogue in the first few weeks instead of spreading it over six months.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Is there a lock-in period or a fixed-term contract?',
    a: 'The monthly plan has no lock-in: it runs for an indefinite term, can be cancelled at any time, and stays usable until your renewal date. The annual plan, by contrast, covers a single, continuous 12-month term paid up front in one instalment: you can cancel at any time, but the cancellation takes effect at the end of the 12 months you paid for, and no pro-rata part of the annual fee is refundable. Neither cycle has a cancellation fee.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What happens to the 6,000 annual credits at the end of the year?',
    a: 'Unused credits expire at the end of the subscription term and do not carry over into the renewed term — a fresh 6,000 credits arrive on renewal. Separately purchased extra credits are independent of this: they stay valid for 365 days from the date of purchase.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I switch from the monthly plan to the annual one?',
    a: 'Yes, at any time, and the switch takes effect immediately. We credit the pro-rata remainder of your paid monthly term towards the annual fee, and any monthly credits you still have are not lost: their expiry is pushed out to the end of the annual term, on top of the 6,000-credit annual allowance. Switching the other way — annual to monthly — only takes effect once the paid 12 months are up.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Is there a smaller, cheaper tier?',
    a: 'No. There is no smaller tier with fewer credits: we offer a single plan that includes every module — you only choose the billing cycle, monthly or annual.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What is an AI credit, and what can 500 of them do?',
    a: 'Credits are the unit we bill AI operations in: every generation (post copy, image, video, newsletter) consumes a set number of credits. One post copy is 1 credit and one Nano Banana image is 2 credits, so a post with an image costs 3 credits — 500 credits a month is roughly 166 posts with images. A blog article costs 3 credits for the copy (plus 2 credits per image in the article), and rewriting a product description is 1 credit per product page (2 credits for a category page). Publishing and scheduling are not AI operations, so they never consume credits.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What happens when I run out of my allowance?',
    a: 'AI-based content generation pauses until your next allowance opens — your next monthly renewal on the monthly plan, or your annual renewal on the annual plan — while the rest of the system (calendar, scheduling, publishing, statistics) keeps working as usual. If you do not want to wait, you can buy extra credits at any time.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How much do extra credits cost, and how long are they valid?',
    a: 'There are two packs to choose from: 500 credits for HUF 14,990 + VAT (HUF 19,037 gross), or, for a bigger project, 5,000 credits for HUF 134,990 + VAT (HUF 171,437 gross, roughly 10% off the credit price). Purchased extra credits are valid for 365 days from the date of purchase and are added on top of your monthly allowance.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Do unused monthly credits roll over to the next month?',
    a: 'No. The 500 credits included in the monthly fee apply to that billing period only; they reset and are topped up again on each renewal date. There is one exception: if you switch to the annual plan, your remaining monthly credits have their expiry pushed out to the end of the annual term. The annual plan\'s 6,000 credits are never reset monthly — they cover the whole 12 months. Separately purchased extra credits stay valid for 365 days regardless. If you cancel your subscription, unused extra credits are also forfeited at the end of the period.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How does payment work?',
    a: 'Payment is made by bank card through Stripe, always in advance: monthly subscriptions are billed every month, annual subscriptions in one instalment at the start of the term. Card details are handled by Stripe, under their own security standards. Invoices are issued to the billing details you provided at registration, so you do not need to enter them again.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How do I change my card or cancel my subscription?',
    a: 'Both are handled in the app once you are signed in to your account. When replacing a card, always add the new payment method first and only then delete the old one. To cancel, open your subscription and confirm the cancellation — you can keep using the system until your renewal date.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I manage several webshops on one subscription?',
    a: 'Yes. A single subscription can hold several brands (webshops), each with its own core information, logo and knowledge sources, and you can connect multiple social media accounts per brand — there is no limit on the number of accounts. For technical reasons we can currently provide one user per subscription.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Do you refund fees already paid?',
    a: 'Subscription fees already paid are non-refundable — this also applies to the annual fee paid up front in one instalment, of which no pro-rata part can be credited back. If you cancel, the service stays active until the end of the period you paid for, so you do not lose what you have already paid.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How can I track my own usage?',
    a: 'The Usage section in the app shows your current credit balance in real time, along with a per-operation consumption history and the expiry date of your extra credits.',
  },
];

const faqLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faqs.map((f) => ({
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: f.q,
    acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: f.a },
  })),
};

const textOps = [
  { op: 'Post copy generation / regeneration', credit: '1' },
  { op: 'Newsletter copy generation / regeneration', credit: '3' },
  { op: 'Blog article copy generation / regeneration', credit: '3' },
  { op: 'Blog deep research (optional, with web search)', credit: '5' },
  { op: 'Product description rewriting (Shopgrade)', credit: '1 / product' },
  { op: 'Category page rewriting (Shopgrade)', credit: '2 / category' },
  { op: 'Ad copy generation / regeneration', credit: '1' },
  { op: 'HTML template generation for newsletters', credit: '2' },
];

const imageOps = [
  { op: 'New AI image (Nano Banana)', credit: '2' },
  { op: 'New AI image (Nano Banana Pro)', credit: '5' },
  { op: 'New AI image (GPT Image)', credit: '5' },
  { op: 'Image resizing (Nano Banana)', credit: '2' },
  { op: 'Image resizing (Nano Banana Pro)', credit: '5' },
  { op: 'Blog article images (cover + embedded, Nano Banana)', credit: '2 / image' },
  { op: 'Short animation from an image (WAN Video)', credit: '2' },
  { op: 'Short animation from an image (Grok Imagine Video)', credit: '1 / sec' },
];

const videoOps = [
  { op: 'Video script generation', credit: '1' },
  { op: 'Video generation', credit: '1 / sec' },
];

const narrationOps = [
  { op: 'Image generation', credit: '2 / image' },
  { op: 'Narration generation', credit: '1' },
  { op: 'Background music generation', credit: '1' },
  { op: 'Subtitle generation', credit: '1' },
  { op: 'Starting the video render + first 30 sec', credit: '5' },
  { op: 'Each further started 30 sec', credit: '4' },
];

const freeOps = [
  'Publishing and scheduling (Facebook, Instagram)',
  'Placing your logo onto an image',
  'Marketing calendar, approvals, editing',
  'Viewing statistics and comments',
];
---

<BaseLayout
  locale={locale}
  page={page}
  title={title}
  description={description}
  keywords={keywords}
  lpEnabled
>
  <script slot="head" type="application/ld+json" is:inline set:html={JSON.stringify(faqLd)} />

  <Header locale={locale} page={page} />

  <main>
    <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════
     HERO
═══════════════════════════════════════ -->
    <section id="hero" class="hero-gradient py-12 md:py-16">
      <div class="max-w-[1200px] mx-auto px-4 md:px-10">
        <div class="max-w-[760px] mx-auto text-center flex flex-col gap-5 animate-fade-up">
          <span class="text-primary font-bold text-sm uppercase tracking-widest block mb-3">PRICING</span>
          <!-- The "from" is precision, not style: HUF 29,158 requires the annual plan;
               on the monthly cycle it is HUF 34,990. -->
          <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.03em] leading-tight">
            One plan <span class="text-primary">for webshops</span>, from
            <span class="text-primary">HUF 29,158 + VAT</span> a month
          </h1>
          <p class="text-body text-lg leading-relaxed">
            Every module is included — posting, blog articles, Shopgrade, newsletters, image and
            video generation.
          </p>

          <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-3 mt-1">
            <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-success/10 border border-success/30 text-success rounded-[10px] px-4 py-2 text-sm font-bold">
              <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-[18px]">savings</span>
              Annual plan: 2 months free
            </span>
            <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-card border border-border rounded-[10px] px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium text-body">
              <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-primary text-[18px]">lock_open</span>
              No lock-in on the monthly plan
            </span>
            <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-card border border-border rounded-[10px] px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium text-body">
              <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-primary text-[18px]">credit_card</span>
              Paid via Stripe
            </span>
          </div>

          <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-center gap-3 mt-4">
            <a href="/en/book-demo/" class="cta-primary px-6 h-12 text-sm w-full sm:w-auto justify-center">
              Book a demo
              <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-[16px]">arrow_forward</span>
            </a>
            <a href="#credits" class="cta-secondary px-6 h-12 text-sm w-full sm:w-auto justify-center">
              Detailed credit costs
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Hitelesitesek: Meta Tech Provider + UNAS partner (kozos komponens) -->
    <TrustBadges locale={locale} />

    <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════
     PLAN
═══════════════════════════════════════ -->
    <section id="plan" class="bg-light py-20 md:py-28">
      <div class="max-w-[900px] mx-auto px-4 md:px-10">
        <div class="text-center mb-14">
          <span class="text-primary font-bold text-sm uppercase tracking-widest block mb-3">THE PLAN</span>
          <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold mb-4">Try it at a lower price!</h2>
          <!-- The "on the monthly plan" is not hair-splitting: the annual plan is a single,
               continuous 12-month term with no pro-rata refund (Terms 4.3, 5.2). -->
          <p class="text-body text-lg">
            If you do not like it, you can cancel any time on the monthly plan. No risk.
          </p>
        </div>

        <PricingCards locale={locale} />
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════
     WHAT 500 CREDITS BUY
═══════════════════════════════════════ -->
    <section id="what-you-get" class="bg-card py-20 md:py-28">
      <div class="max-w-[1200px] mx-auto px-4 md:px-10">
        <div class="text-center mb-14">
          <span class="text-primary font-bold text-sm uppercase tracking-widest block mb-3">WORKED EXAMPLES</span>
          <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold mb-4">What do 500 credits a month buy?</h2>
          <p class="text-body text-lg">Six typical uses — if you spent the whole allowance on just one thing.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-8 mb-8">
          {[
            {
              icon: 'edit_note',
              title: '≈ 166 posts with images',
              detail: 'Post copy (1) + Nano Banana image (2) = 3 credits per post',
            },
            {
              icon: 'article',
              title: '≈ 71 blog articles',
              detail: 'Article copy (3) + 2 Nano Banana images (2×2) = 7 credits per article. Deep research is optional, +5.',
            },
            {
              icon: 'edit_document',
              title: '≈ 500 product descriptions',
              detail: 'Shopgrade: 1 credit per product page, 2 credits per category page – in bulk too.',
            },
            {
              icon: 'mail',
              title: '≈ 100 newsletters',
              detail: 'Newsletter copy (3) + one Nano Banana image (2) = 5 credits per e-mail. The HTML template only needs generating once.',
            },
            {
              icon: 'movie',
              title: '≈ 25 narrated videos',
              detail: 'A one-minute video with 4 images = 20 credits each',
            },
            {
              icon: 'image',
              title: '≈ 250 AI images',
              detail: 'A Nano Banana image costs 2 credits — on-brand, logo-stamped creative.',
            },
          ].map((card) => (
            <div class="bg-light rounded-[16px] border border-border p-8 shadow-card hover:shadow-card-hover transition-all">
              <div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-[12px] bg-primary/10 flex items-center justify-center mb-5">
                <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-primary text-[22px]">{card.icon}</span>
              </div>
              <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-dark mb-2">{card.title}</h3>
              <p class="text-body text-sm leading-relaxed">{card.detail}</p>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>

        <div class="bg-light rounded-[16px] border border-border p-5 sm:p-8 shadow-card">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-dark mb-4">A realistic, mixed month</h3>
          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-4 text-sm">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-body">
              <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-primary text-[20px]">edit_note</span>
              <span>15 posts with images (3–4 a week) <strong class="text-dark">45</strong></span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-body">
              <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-primary text-[20px]">article</span>
              <span>5 blog articles, with images <strong class="text-dark">35</strong></span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-body">
              <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-primary text-[20px]">edit_document</span>
              <span>350 product descriptions rewritten <strong class="text-dark">350</strong></span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-body">
              <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-primary text-[20px]">mail</span>
              <span>6 newsletters <strong class="text-dark">30</strong></span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-body">
              <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-primary text-[20px]">movie</span>
              <span>2 narrated videos <strong class="text-dark">40</strong></span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2 font-bold text-dark">
              <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-success text-[20px]">check_circle</span>
              <span>500 credits in total</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="text-muted text-sm mt-4">
            Publishing all of this is unlimited and free on top. The Usage section in the app
            shows your balance in real time.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- The annual allowance: the same number of credits, but no monthly ceiling -->
        <div class="bg-primary/5 rounded-[16px] border border-primary/20 p-5 sm:p-8 mt-8">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-dark mb-2">And what do the 6,000 annual credits buy?</h3>
          <p class="text-body text-sm leading-relaxed mb-5">
            Exactly as much as 12 months of the monthly allowance — the difference is that
            <strong class="text-dark">there is no monthly ceiling</strong>: the whole allowance
            lands on day one and you spread it over the 12 months however you like. That is what
            makes room for a big opening push you would otherwise have to ration over six months:
          </p>
          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-4 text-sm">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-body">
              <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-primary text-[20px]">edit_document</span>
              <span>3,000 product descriptions at launch <strong class="text-dark">3,000</strong></span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-body">
              <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-primary text-[20px]">category</span>
              <span>200 category pages <strong class="text-dark">400</strong></span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-body">
              <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-primary text-[20px]">article</span>
              <span>40 blog articles, with images <strong class="text-dark">280</strong></span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-body">
              <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-primary text-[20px]">edit_note</span>
              <span>180 posts with images (3–4 a week, all year) <strong class="text-dark">540</strong></span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-body">
              <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-primary text-[20px]">mail</span>
              <span>48 newsletters (one a week) <strong class="text-dark">240</strong></span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-body">
              <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-primary text-[20px]">movie</span>
              <span>24 narrated videos (two a month) <strong class="text-dark">480</strong></span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-body">
              <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-primary text-[20px]">inventory_2</span>
              <span>reserve for seasonal campaigns <strong class="text-dark">1,060</strong></span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2 font-bold text-dark">
              <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-success text-[20px]">check_circle</span>
              <span>6,000 credits in total</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════
     CREDITS – DETAILED COSTS
═══════════════════════════════════════ -->
    <section id="credits" class="bg-light py-20 md:py-28 scroll-mt-24">
      <div class="max-w-[900px] mx-auto px-4 md:px-10">
        <div class="text-center mb-14">
          <span class="text-primary font-bold text-sm uppercase tracking-widest block mb-3">CREDIT COSTS</span>
          <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold mb-4">What does each operation cost?</h2>
          <p class="text-body text-lg leading-relaxed">
            Every AI operation consumes a set number of credits. Each run counts as a new
            operation, and if you use several features at once, the credits add up.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Example -->
        <div class="bg-primary/5 rounded-[16px] border border-primary/20 p-5 sm:p-8 mb-10">
          <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-dark mb-4">Example: one post with an AI image</h3>
          <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center gap-3 sm:gap-5 text-sm">
            <span class="text-body">Post copy <strong class="text-dark">1 credit</strong></span>
            <span class="text-muted hidden sm:inline">+</span>
            <span class="text-body">AI image (Nano Banana) <strong class="text-dark">2 credits</strong></span>
            <span class="text-muted hidden sm:inline">+</span>
            <span class="text-body">logo on the image <strong class="text-success">free</strong></span>
            <span class="text-muted hidden sm:inline">=</span>
            <span class="font-bold text-primary">3 credits in total</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Tables -->
        <div class="space-y-8">
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-dark mb-4">Text generation</h3>
            <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-[12px] border border-border">
              <table class="w-full text-sm">
                <thead>
                  <tr class="bg-light">
                    <th class="text-left font-bold text-dark px-4 py-3 border-b border-border">Operation</th>
                    <th class="text-right font-bold text-dark px-4 py-3 border-b border-border whitespace-nowrap">Credits</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  {textOps.map((row) => (
                    <tr class="border-b border-border last:border-b-0">
                      <td class="px-4 py-3 text-body">{row.op}</td>
                      <td class="px-4 py-3 text-dark font-bold text-right whitespace-nowrap">{row.credit}</td>
                    </tr>
                  ))}
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-dark mb-4">Image generation and editing</h3>
            <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-[12px] border border-border">
              <table class="w-full text-sm">
                <thead>
                  <tr class="bg-light">
                    <th class="text-left font-bold text-dark px-4 py-3 border-b border-border">Operation</th>
                    <th class="text-right font-bold text-dark px-4 py-3 border-b border-border whitespace-nowrap">Credits</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  {imageOps.map((row) => (
                    <tr class="border-b border-border last:border-b-0">
                      <td class="px-4 py-3 text-body">{row.op}</td>
                      <td class="px-4 py-3 text-dark font-bold text-right whitespace-nowrap">{row.credit}</td>
                    </tr>
                  ))}
                  <tr class="border-b border-border last:border-b-0 bg-success/5">
                    <td class="px-4 py-3 text-body">Placing your logo onto an image</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-3 text-success font-bold text-right whitespace-nowrap">free</td>
                  </tr>
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-dark mb-4">Video generation</h3>
            <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-[12px] border border-border">
              <table class="w-full text-sm">
                <thead>
                  <tr class="bg-light">
                    <th class="text-left font-bold text-dark px-4 py-3 border-b border-border">Operation</th>
                    <th class="text-right font-bold text-dark px-4 py-3 border-b border-border whitespace-nowrap">Credits</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  {videoOps.map((row) => (
                    <tr class="border-b border-border last:border-b-0">
                      <td class="px-4 py-3 text-body">{row.op}</td>
                      <td class="px-4 py-3 text-dark font-bold text-right whitespace-nowrap">{row.credit}</td>
                    </tr>
                  ))}
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-dark mb-4">Narrated video generation</h3>
            <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-[12px] border border-border">
              <table class="w-full text-sm">
                <thead>
                  <tr class="bg-light">
                    <th class="text-left font-bold text-dark px-4 py-3 border-b border-border">Operation</th>
                    <th class="text-right font-bold text-dark px-4 py-3 border-b border-border whitespace-nowrap">Credits</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  {narrationOps.map((row) => (
                    <tr class="border-b border-border last:border-b-0">
                      <td class="px-4 py-3 text-body">{row.op}</td>
                      <td class="px-4 py-3 text-dark font-bold text-right whitespace-nowrap">{row.credit}</td>
                    </tr>
                  ))}
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </div>
            <p class="text-muted text-sm mt-3">
              A one-minute narrated video with 4 images therefore costs
              <strong class="text-dark">20 credits</strong> in total (4×2 images + 1 narration +
